# Install devDependencies here even when NODE_ENV says production.
#
# This project is TypeScript, so the BUILD needs typescript and every @types/*
# package — and all of them are devDependencies, which is where they belong.
# Render sets NODE_ENV=production, npm then skips devDependencies, and the
# compiler runs with no idea what `process`, `console` or `express` are. That
# is about eighty errors from one cause.
#
# The build command in render.yaml passes --include=dev for the same reason.
# This file is the belt to that pair of braces: a service created by hand in
# the Render dashboard ignores render.yaml completely, and then the only place
# left to say this is the repository.
#
# `npm prune --omit=dev` after the build takes them out again, so nothing extra
# ships.
include=dev
